codex
The patch fixes the nested-module false red, but introduces a false green for valid Rust files with a leading shebang before a file-level cfg attribute. That can allow pinned test proofs to be compiled out without the gate detecting it.

Review comment:

- [P2] Treat a leading Rust shebang as part of the header — /home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/orch-0.8.20-s30/scripts/check-c1-conformance.sh:1865-1868
  If a pinned Rust test file starts with a valid shebang line, this loop stops before reading any following file-level inner attributes, so `#!/...` followed by `#![cfg(feature = "...")]` disables the whole test file while the conformance check still exits 0. The previous whole-file scan caught that case; the narrowed header scan should skip a leading shebang before deciding there are no file-level `#![...]` attrs.
